:not() with a selector LIST                          REACHED          canary=cascaded drops=[-]
@layer (block form)                                  REACHED          canary=cascaded drops=[-]
@layer ORDER (declared precedence)                   WRONG WINNER     display=5 (hi=flex=3, lo=grid=5): both layers cascaded, but the LOW layer won because it is later -- layer precedence is source order, the declared order is ignored
@container (query entered)                           REACHED          canary=cascaded drops=[container-type(0)]
@container (a FALSE query must not apply)            ALWAYS-TRUE      display=5: a query no container can satisfy (min-width:100000px against a 50px container) APPLIED ANYWAY -- @container is ENTERED, never evaluated
@property initial-value reaches var()                RULE LOST        width=0 has_w=0, want 100 from initial-value: the initial-value never reached var(--pw). The at-rule does not swallow the sheet, but its registration is discarded.
@scope confines its rules to the scope root          ALWAYS-TRUE      inside .ctx display=3, OUTSIDE .ctx display=3: the scoped rule applied outside its scope root
